Minato's patch to frameworks/base's core/java/android/provider/DocumentsContract.java at android-15.0.0_r1
(Apache-2.0), framework breadth F4a: DOWNLOADS_PROVIDER_AUTHORITY is the literal.

Why: the constant is Downloads.Impl.AUTHORITY, which is the string "downloads". Downloads (the download provider's
contract) imports NetworkPolicyManager and DownloadManager's hidden actions, which Minato has no use for: it has no
download provider. A constant of a String is inlined by javac, so the literal is the same value at run time as
Android's class gives.

--- a/core/java/android/provider/DocumentsContract.java
+++ b/core/java/android/provider/DocumentsContract.java
@@ -249,7 +249,7 @@
      * {@hide}
      */
     @SystemApi
-    public static final String DOWNLOADS_PROVIDER_AUTHORITY = Downloads.Impl.AUTHORITY;
+    public static final String DOWNLOADS_PROVIDER_AUTHORITY = "downloads";
 
     /** {@hide} */
     public static final String EXTERNAL_STORAGE_PRIMARY_EMULATED_ROOT_ID = "primary";
